From afdd3b1bd7f7f5f94f6497405b3a2938c7fa1209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moritz Hoffmann <antiguru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 15:16:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve the D10 spike so its measurements can be audited

The spike crate as it stood when the numbers in d10-decision.md were taken.
Task 3.1 Step 5 says to delete it, and 43c4ba5f did, which left the LOC
comparison, the throughput gap and the 27/27 error-fidelity result with nothing
behind them. This branch exists only so a reader can re-run them; it is not
merged and plan/rust-rewrite does not carry the crate.

Reproduce, from the rust/ directory:

  cargo test --offline -p rexx-parse-spike
  cargo run --offline --release -p rexx-parse-spike --example throughput

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Lgr1Bubd4xCGLNC2igi6Ak
